dot(origin);
dot((1,0));
dot((0,1));
dot((0,0));

fill((0,0)--(1,0)--(0,1)--cycle,rgb(0.81,1,0));
label("$(1,0)$",(1,0),SW);
label("$(0,1)$",(0,1),NE);
[/asy] \[\begin{array}{cc}
(0, 0) \\
(0, 1) &  \\
(1, 0) &
\end{array}\] The sides of the octagon have slopes $-1$ and 1.  Points on the octagon will be a distance 1 from the origin by the distance formula.  By properties of similar right triangles, the length of the perpendicular to the hypotenuse formed by the line containing one of the vertices of the octagon intersects the line containing the vertex one-quarter of the length of the smaller side away from the vertex on the octagon.  This results in the following right triangle with sides in proportion 3:4:5.

